== #2540 Felton School [places]
body: Before the school opened, children in the Pico Canyon oil field were sent to Newhall to be educated. The Felton School opened its doors in October 1885, named for Charles Felton, president of the Pacific Coast Oil Company. Keeping the five pupils the Felton School District needed to continue was a recurring difficulty through the last years of the Pico Canyon field. The district was absorbed into the Newhall School District in 1933, after again falling short of the five-student minimum.
